CHAPTER VIII

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 36

1. The community may participate in assisting prevention and handling efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is in the form of: a. providing information and or reporting any violence known;
b. providing protection for victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;T 17d. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding the handling of gender-based violence and violence against children;
e. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders; f. assisting in the repatriation and social reintegration process.
3. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

Article 12

1. The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement efforts to protect victims of violence in the form of:

a. preventing the occurrence of all forms of gender-based and child violence;

b. providing protection by providing complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal assistance and enforcement services, repatriation and social reintegration services, seeking to increase community participation, as well as monitoring and reporting;

c. encouraging and increasing community participation;

d. cooperating with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence.

(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:

a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based and child violence;

b. establish an integrated service center;

c. establish complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;

d. facilitate the implementation of integrated service centers and activities of complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;

e. provide facilities and infrastructure;

f. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;

g. coordinate and cooperate in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based and child violence;

h. encourage and increase community participation;

i. conduct monitoring and evaluation.

3. In carrying out its obligations, responsibilities and authorities, the Regent may delegate to related SKPD.

4. Related SKPD that receive delegation from the Regent as referred to in paragraph (3) in its implementation shall prepare a Regional Action Plan for the protection of victims.

Article 16

PPT PKBGA as referred to in Article 14 letter a has the duties:

a. seeking prevention;

b. providing complaint services;

c. providing health services;

d. providing social rehabilitation services;

e. providing legal assistance and enforcement services;

f. providing repatriation and social reintegration services;

g. conducting coordination and cooperation;

h. seeking to increase community participation;

i. conducting monitoring and reporting.

Article 3

The Objectives of Victim Protection are to:

a. prevent all forms of gender-based violence and violence against children, occurring within the scope of the household and/or community;
b. provide protection in the form of complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal assistance and enforcement services, as well as repatriation and social reintegration services;
c. seek to increase community participation.

Article 32

1. Every victim of gender-based violence and violence against children has the right to: a. obtain protection for personal, family and property security, and be free from threats related to information that will be, is being, or has been given; b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
c. be free from ensnaring questions;
d. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
e. obtain complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal assistance and enforcement services, as well as repatriation and social reintegration services.
2. The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

REGENT OF BANYUMAS

PROVINCE OF CENTRAL JAVA

REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANYUMAS REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2015

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION

VICTIMS OF GENDER-BASED AND CHILD VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF BANYUMAS,

Considering:
a. that all forms of violence, especially gender-based and child violence constitute violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity;
b. that victims of gender-based and child violence in the Region continue to increase;
c. that victims of violence need to be protected in their dignity and honor and guaranteed their right to life in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
d. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based and child violence;
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based and Child Violence;

In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of Central Java;
